ody-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:23201c8775268dfa59835b4b5c15dec09490216d3813ed89e4b4ac8b2351c406","file":"preprints/One-Rational-Matrix-Hitting-Point-for-Noncommutative-Formulas-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":24,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"165b53bdd33ea412ba0dd51804fd48178b2c17aaa7c06b1e62e1a56e977f8545","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/One-Rational-Matrix-Hitting-Point-for-Noncommutative-Formulas-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:23201c8775268dfa59835b4b5c15dec09490216d3813ed89e4b4ac8b2351c406","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/One-Rational-Matrix-Hitting-Point-for-Noncommutative-Formulas-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L24"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is a deterministic algorithm which, given integers $n,s\\ge1$,\nconstructs a tuple\n\\[\n \\mathbf T_{n,s}\\in\\Mat_d(\\Q)^n,\n \\qquad d\\le 2ns^2,\n\\]\nin time polynomial in $n,s$, measured in bit operations. The numerators and\ndenominators of its entries have bit length\n$O(\\log(ns+1)+ns^2\\log(n+1))$.\nFor every field $F$ of characteristic zero and every\n$0\\ne f\\in\\mathsf{Form}_{n,s}(F)$,\n\\[\n f(\\mathbf T_{n,s})\\ne0,\n\\]\nwhere the tuple is viewed over $F$ through the canonical embedding\n$\\Q\\hookrightarrow F$. The construction uses $d=2ns^2$ when $ns\\ge2$\nand $d=1$ when $n=s=1$."}
